course: dictionary
lesson: 11109
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Whirl can mean spin fast, move quickly, or try something. The words around it show you which meaning to use. «The dancers whirled across the floor.» Here whirl means moving quickly, and the dancers are probably turning too.
explain: «Her thoughts were in a whirl.» A mind cannot spin, so this is a picture. It means her head was confused, because too much was happening at once. Ask yourself what would make sense if you put your own meaning in place of the hard word.
explain: «Let's give it a whirl!» means let's try it. This is informal, so you would say it to a friend, not write it in a science report. When you meet a word with several meanings, test each one in the sentence and pick the one that fits best.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Whirl» means turn or spin round and round very fast, as in «the leaves whirl in the wind».
fact: «Whirl» can also mean move somewhere very quickly, as in «the dancers whirled across the floor».
fact: «In a whirl» means confused because too much is happening, and «give it a whirl» means try it (informal).
fact: A whirl is a fast spinning movement, and it is also a noun, as in «a whirl of dust».
exercise: «The leaves whirled in the autumn wind.» What does whirled mean here? | Fell slowly and gently | Were kept safe in a box | *Spun round and round very fast | Turned bright red
exercise: Maya says, «Let's give it a whirl!» What does she mean? | Let's go home now | Let's be sad together | Let's spin around the park | *Let's try it
exercise: «My thoughts were in a whirl after the news.» What does in a whirl suggest? | Calm and quiet | Wet and grey | Very hungry | *Confused, with too much happening
test: «The dancers whirled across the floor.» Which meaning fits whirled here? | *Moved somewhere very quickly | Slept on the floor | Sat very still | Fell asleep
test: Which sentence uses whirl as a noun? | *A whirl of dust rose from the road | Dad will whirl the eggs | We whirled round the field | The leaves whirl in the wind
exam: In «Her head was in a whirl», what does whirl mean? | Spinning round the room | Quiet and calm | *Confused, with too much happening | Very hungry
